WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.100
-Welcome back, everybody.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.868
We are here with
Samuel L. Jackson!

00:00:03.868 --> 00:00:05.701
Now, come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.901
Samuel, you have a career
that spans decades

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:10.033
of both Oscar-winning movies,
some of the most

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:11.467
famous franchises of all time.

00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:12.634
You've seen it all.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.200
I thought that you could help me
settle some of

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.534
the biggest and most important
debates ever.

00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:18.634
Are you ready to do this?
-No fear.

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:20.434
-Alright, It's time for
"Samuel L. Jackson Settles It."

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:22.434
-♪ "Samuel L. Jackson
Settles It" ♪

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:25.000
♪ "Samuel L. Jackson
Settles It" ♪

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.133
-There you go, bud.
Alright, here we go.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:31.701
First up, is it...

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:34.601
-[ Laughs ] "Pee-can" pie
or "pe-cahn"?

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.033
Is that what you said?
-"Pe-cahn."

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.634
-"Pe-cahn."
-"Pe-cahn."

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:38.767
-"Pe-cahn."
-"Pe-cahn" pie.

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:42.901
-Uh, "pee-can" pie
if you're from the South,

00:00:42.901 --> 00:00:45.033
"pe-cahn" pie
if you're from the North.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:47.767
-Ah! Alright, alright.

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:50.033
"Pe-cahn" pie.

00:00:52.234 --> 00:00:54.567
-Real.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:58.734
You've got to have
that pine smell in the house.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:00.100
You know, you got to smell it.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.968
You can't smell that
tinsel tree,

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:03.367
that aluminum thing
that people put up.

00:01:03.367 --> 00:01:06.100
-I had a fake thing
in my house for years.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.901
My whole life, growing up,
I had the same Christmas tree.

00:01:07.901 --> 00:01:10.634
It was in the basement.
and every time we pulled it out,

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:12.501
it's this musty smell,

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:14.200
and that is the smell
of Christmas for me.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.901
-That is so bad. No.
-Alright.

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:21.234
-Homemade stuffing!
Come on. Stove Top? What?!

00:01:21.234 --> 00:01:22.267
-What?!
-What?!

00:01:22.267 --> 00:01:23.467
-Really?

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:26.300
-Stove Top stuffing --
I mean, the city dwellers

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:30.234
who never had to cook at home or
never had a real kitchen

00:01:30.234 --> 00:01:34.000
or never wanted to smell
the food cooking all day --

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.534
See, you've got to have that
smell all day.

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:39.067
You can't just have it Stove Top
quick, quick, quick.

00:01:39.067 --> 00:01:40.367
No.
-No. It's got to go all the way.

00:01:40.367 --> 00:01:42.100
Alright. Good.
I like the homemade.

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:46.234
Oh, come on.
-On what?

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:49.200
On a plane?
-Yeah.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.400
-Oh, people get choices?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:56.234
If I'm on a --
Well, I like an aisle seat

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:57.901
because I don't like
crawling over people,

00:01:57.901 --> 00:02:00.100
when I used to fly
with other people.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.601
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:06.267
Wow! Wow! You really...

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:09.400
Wow! That's the old
Samuel -- Yeah.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.100
-Well, you have to adjust --

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.968
The times, you adjust --

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:16.801
You fix your contract perks
so that you...

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:18.667
-Yeah. Very smart man.
-...don't fly with other people.

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:19.801
-I know.

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:26.200
-Ooh, fries.
-Yeah.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.167
Sautéed onions.
-Oh, really?

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:31.567
-Sautéed onions.
You know...

00:02:31.567 --> 00:02:33.534
-That'll spruce 'em up.
-Yeah.

00:02:37.133 --> 00:02:39.167
-The original "Star Wars."
-Okay.

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:42.100
-Yeah. I mean,
there's nothing like --

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.100
That was the first time --
You know, I remember

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.334
watching that film on,
like, 44th Street.

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:48.801
I was, like, at the
second screening or something.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.334
When they go into hyperspace
for the first time,

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:53.434
that was like,
"Oh, my God, what was that?"

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:54.634
-"I've never seen
anything like that."

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:55.968
-Plus, I mean,
that was like during the time

00:02:55.968 --> 00:02:57.267
when you had,
like, horrible weed

00:02:57.267 --> 00:02:58.701
and you had, like,
little nickel bags.

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.734
And you're sitting there
and you're like...

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.868
And then they go "Da-da-da"
and they hit it.

00:03:02.868 --> 00:03:06.667
-Yeah, yeah.
-Everybody's like, "Whoaaa!"

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:10.234
It was like the bomb.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:12.501
It was all that. Yeah.

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:16.033
-And, finally, let's figure this
out once and for all.

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:18.200
What is the best curse word?

00:03:22.434 --> 00:03:24.968
-The best curse word.
Damn, that's hard to say.

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:26.634
[ Drumroll ]

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:29.767
I mean, I love my favorite
because it's my favorite,

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:32.901
but everybody
doesn't do it great.

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:37.100
And -- I don't know, man.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.267
It's like --
There's so many good ones.

00:03:39.267 --> 00:03:41.601
-There's a lot of good ones.
-Yeah.

00:03:41.601 --> 00:03:43.501
You know, the ones with
one syllable

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:46.300
aren't as good as the ones
with two and three syllables.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:48.100
-Yeah, four syllables --

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.300
-So if you got --
The more syllables you have,

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.334
the better the curse word.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.934
-Like a "enh-enh, enh-enh."

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:54.367
-Mm-hmm.
-"Enh-enh, enh-enh."

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:57.300
-Yeah, right. You know.
-So, we would say --

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.934
-Well, you know,
rather than saying --

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:03.367
"Sum'bitch" is not good as
"son of a bitch!"

00:04:03.367 --> 00:04:05.234
-Yeah!
-You know?

00:04:05.234 --> 00:04:08.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.734
It's all about the syllables.
There you have it.

00:04:09.734 --> 00:04:11.634
Samuel L. Jackson.

